<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17531" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">factor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				maker</i>, <i>doer</i>, <i>performer</i>, <i>perpetrator</i> (ante- and
			postclass.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cuparum doliorumque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui praepositum suum non praetexit, cum posset,
					in pari causa factori habendus est,</span>”
				<i>the doer</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 49, 16, 6, § 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sceleris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 29, 5, 1, § 21</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">48, 3, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suus,</span>”
				<i>his creator</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Deut. 32, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Isa. 29, 16 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legis,</span>”
				<i>doer</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rom. 2, 13</span></i>
			; id. Jacob, 1, 23.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In econom. lang., <i>an oil-presser</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 13</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">66</span></i>; 67.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In ball-playing, <i>he who strikes the ball</i>, <i>the
				batsman</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 2, 3, 18</span></i>; cf.
		dator.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
